        <mxCell id="note_alert_hop" value="Hop Breakdown: Hop 1: Sensor to Node (10 s) -&gt; Hop 2: Radio Attach/TLS (60 s) -&gt; Hop 3: MQTT to PUBACK (20 s) -&gt; Hop 4: Rule to SQS (10 s) -&gt; Hop 5: Lambda (20 s) -&gt; Hop 6: SNS (30 s) -&gt; Hop 7: Notification to Phone (60 s) = 210 s Target (90 s margin to 300 s limit)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ecfdf5;strokeColor=#10b981;fontColor=#065f46;fontSize=12;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2130" y="925" width="1470" height="45" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="grp_table" value="5. SUMMARY OF CONNECTIVITY FLOWS &amp; TRACEABILITY TO TRACK B  (docs/connectivity.md Section 3 &amp; docs/architecture.md Section 14)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#475569;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=17;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1180" width="3620" height="1080" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card_60_1230" value="FLOW 1: FARM (CROP ZONE)&#10;&#10;Actor &amp; Device: Crop node, energy autonomous (solar+battery, ASM-070)&#10;Exit Protocol: MQTT 3.1.1/5 over TLS 1.2+, X.509 client cert, port 8883 (443 ALPN alt), QoS 1&#10;Local Buffer: Non-volatile ring buffer, max retention 24 hours (ASM-074)&#10;Without Signal: Store-and-forward; on reconnect, live reading sent first, then oldest drained&#10;Cloud Endpoint: AWS IoT Core regional endpoint in us-east-1, public (D09)&#10;Alert Path: IoT Rule -&gt; SQS -&gt; Threshold Lambda (D10) -&gt; SNS -&gt; Farmer Phone (&lt;5 min, 210 s target)&#10;Bypasses Collection Center and VPC subnets (telemetry_ingress is reserved for interface endpoints)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="1230" width="880" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card_960_1230" value="FLOW 2: FARM OUT OF COVERAGE&#10;&#10;Actor &amp; Device: Crop &amp; drying nodes with dual-mode cellular + satellite module (ASM-073)&#10;Exit Protocol: Same MQTT over TLS with X.509 cert over satellite IP bearer&#10;Local Buffer: Same 24 h non-volatile buffer; contact interval &lt;= 4 hours&#10;Without Signal: Readings wait in buffer for next satellite contact pass (within 24 h)&#10;Cloud Endpoint: Same AWS IoT Core regional endpoint and topic in us-east-1 (No cloud redesign)&#10;Farmer Alert: Alert raised in cloud on contact; reaches farmer when phone enters data coverage&#10;Opens drone confirmation case immediately (crop_alert_raised) without waiting for farmer." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="960" y="1230" width="880" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card_1860_1230" value="FLOW 3: WET MILL (DRYING &amp; SACKS)&#10;&#10;Actor &amp; Device: Drying node (hourly reading); Farmer smartphone &amp; app&#10;Exit Protocol: Drying node: MQTT over TLS (same as farm). Farmer app: HTTPS TLS 1.2+&#10;Local Buffer: Drying node: 24 h buffer. Farmer app: Encrypted outbox until persistence ACK (ASM-079)&#10;Without Signal: Drying: Store-and-forward 24 h. Farmer app: Outbox holds sack registration&#10;Cloud Endpoint: Drying -&gt; IoT Core. Farmer app -&gt; CloudFront / Public App API -&gt; application tier&#10;Custody Resilience: Transporter can accept custody by scanning sack even if farm upload is delayed." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1860" y="1230" width="880" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card_2760_1230" value="FLOW 4: CONTRACTED DRONE OPERATOR&#10;&#10;Actor &amp; Device: Contracted operator drone and ground station (ADR-002, ASM-023)&#10;Exit Protocol: HTTPS TLS 1.2+; Mission download via API; Flight record &amp; imagery upload to S3&#10;Local Buffer: Storage of drone and ground station; no time limit; fumigation cannot close until persisted&#10;Without Signal: Mission preloaded; flight proceeds; record/objects buffered until reconnect&#10;Path from Center: Ground station on Soporte (10.4x.2.10) -&gt; IPsec VPN -&gt; transit -&gt; application &amp; object_storage S3 interface endpoints (CC-DRN-01/03). (drone_object_ingress tier holds no endpoint in pilot, ASM-140!)&#10;Path from Municipal Seat: Public data link -&gt; Public internet -&gt; Public S3 (presigned URL) &amp; API." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2760" y="1230" width="880" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card_60_1450" value="FLOW 5: TRANSPORTER EN ROUTE &amp; YARD&#10;&#10;Actor &amp; Device: Transporter smartphone and mobile app (ASM-076, ASM-079)&#10;Exit Protocol: HTTPS TLS 1.2+; GNSS fix every 5 min en route; transport_position &amp; sack_custody&#10;Local Buffer: Encrypted outbox (7 days capacity, 2,016 fixes); custody events never evicted&#10;Without Signal: GNSS fixes continue without data; on reconnect, custody uploaded first, then positions&#10;Cloud Endpoint: CloudFront / Public Application API -&gt; application tier&#10;Collection Center Yard: Optional connection to cc-transport SSID (10.4x.4.0/24); uses local internet breakout directly to Public API; does NOT traverse the IPsec VPN tunnel (CC-TEL-02)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="1450" width="880" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card_960_1450" value="FLOW 6: COLLECTION CENTER WAN &amp; OPERATIONS&#10;&#10;Actor &amp; Device: Logistics reception posts, desktops, code-sheet printers, and center firewall&#10;Exit Protocol: IPsec site-to-site VPN (2 tunnels over 100 Mbps WAN + cellular backup, ASM-078)&#10;Local Buffer: Encrypted outbox on each logistics post; releases on persistence ACK (ASM-079)&#10;Without WAN: Reception continues offline; events buffer locally; RADIUS validates via cached CRL&#10;Cloud Endpoint: Hub -&gt; transit tier -&gt; pdn application (CC-LOG-01) &amp; administration (CC-ADM-01/02)&#10;Printing &amp; Breakout: Code sheets print locally on VLAN 110 (CC-LOG-02); Guest/yard break out to web." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="960" y="1450" width="880" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card_1860_1450" value="FLOW 7: PORT OF BUENAVENTURA&#10;&#10;Actor &amp; Device: Transporter smartphone and app (ASM-077); No Federation equipment deployed&#10;Exit Protocol: HTTPS TLS 1.2+ over public cellular network&#10;Local Buffer: Transporter app encrypted outbox; keeps original recorded_at timestamp&#10;Without Signal: Event waits in outbox; uploads on data reconnect&#10;Cloud Endpoint: CloudFront / Public Application API -&gt; application tier&#10;Event Recorded: sack_custody with outcome=accepted/rejected and receiver reference; closes trip." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1860" y="1450" width="880" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card_2760_1450" value="TRACK B TRACEABILITY BADGES (D01-D13)&#10;&#10;[D04] VPC and Tiers of Pattern Environment: Addressing plan sec 3,4; Firewall rules; 10.82.0.0/16&#10;[D05] Center Association: 10.40.0.0/13 summary, IPsec VPN tunnels, TGW Hub in Network Acct&#10;[D07] Pattern Firewall Rules: Center firewall (CC rules) &amp; VPC security controls (CL rules)&#10;[D08] Reusable Farm Module: Pattern farm crop/drying nodes, 24 h buffer, satellite dual-mode&#10;[D09] Telemetry Ingestion: AWS IoT Core regional endpoint, mutual X.509, idempotent DynamoDB&#10;[D10] Event-Driven Inference: Threshold Lambda, SQS queue, SNS alert pipeline (&lt;5 min budget)&#10;Azure: 10.88.0.0/13 Prepared, not deployed secondary cloud export target (ADR-001)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#d97706;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#92400e;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2760" y="1450" width="880" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="banner_principles" value="ARCHITECTURAL CONTRACT &amp; DESIGN PRINCIPLES (docs/connectivity.md Section 2):&#10;1. Identity, Not Address: Field devices and phones hold no cloud private IP; authenticated by X.509 certs or IAM/Cognito. Scaling from 200 to 1,000 farms needs no re-addressing.&#10;2. Bearer Neutrality: IP bearer carrying TLS only; no dependency on 2G/3G or legacy circuit-switched mobile generations (ASM-072, PD-080).&#10;3. Original Timestamp &amp; Idempotency: Every buffered record carries creation time and idempotency key (node_id + timestamp or event_id). Drained record evaluated as if live.&#10;4. Release on Acknowledgement: Records leave local buffer ONLY after verified cloud ACK (MQTT PUBACK, HTTP 2xx, or S3 checksum). Duplicate delivery is harmlessly absorbed.&#10;5. End-to-End Encryption: TLS 1.2+ end-to-end; no intermediate gateway terminates TLS or inspects payloads. Buffers encrypted at rest." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#334155;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="1680" width="3580" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="banner_latency" value="CROP ALERT LATENCY BUDGET BREAKDOWN (&lt; 5 MINUTES / 300 SECONDS CASE STATEMENT TARGET) - docs/connectivity.md Section 8.2:&#10;Hop 1: Reading taken to message ready on node (10 s)  --&gt;  Hop 2: Radio wake, network attach &amp; TLS connection (60 s)  --&gt;  Hop 3: MQTT publish to broker PUBACK at IoT Core (20 s)  --&gt;  Hop 4: Topic rule to SQS threshold queue invocation (10 s)&#10;Hop 5: Threshold Lambda evaluates ranges, writes DB &amp; publishes SNS (20 s)  --&gt;  Hop 6: SNS topic to notification provider (30 s)  --&gt;  Hop 7: Provider to Farmer Phone (60 s)  |  TOTAL TARGET: 210 s  |  MARGIN: 90 s  |  CASE LIMIT: 300 s" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ecfdf5;strokeColor=#059669;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#065f46;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="1830" width="3580" height="95" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="banner_compliance" value="NORMATIVE REFERENCES &amp; REPOSITORY BOUNDARIES (aroma-pacifico-diagrams network/):&#10;- Source documents: docs/connectivity.md (all sections), docs/collection-center-network.md, docs/firewall-policy.md section 4 in aroma-pacifico-architecture (main).&#10;- Traceability to IaC: Box catalog in docs/architecture.md section 14 (D04 VPC/Tiers, D05 Center Association, D07 Firewall Rules, D08 Farm Module, D09 Telemetry, D10 Inference Functions).&#10;- Strict No-Signal Constraints: Telemetry buffer max 24 h (ASM-074); App outbox releases on ACK only (ASM-079); Drone buffers until reconnect without flight closure (ADR-002).&#10;- Private vs Public Path Separation: Farm telemetry and transporter traffic never cross center VPN; drone_object_ingress tier holds no endpoint in pilot (ASM-140)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#d97706;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#92400e;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="1945" width="3580" height="95" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="banner_legend" value="DIAGRAM LEGEND &amp; CONNECTOR KEY:&#10;---&gt; Green/Teal Line: Telemetry &amp; Sensor Path (MQTT/TLS direct to IoT Core public endpoint; bypasses centers and VPC)&#10;---&gt; Blue Line: Application &amp; Logistics Flow (HTTPS TLS 1.2+ to CloudFront/Public API or via IPsec VPN to private endpoints)&#10;---&gt; Purple Line: Drone Mission &amp; Imagery Path (Preloaded mission, private S3 multipart upload via object_storage endpoint)&#10;---&gt; Amber/Orange Line: WAN &amp; Site-to-Site IPsec VPN (Dual tunnels over 100 Mbps WAN + cellular backup to TGW Hub)&#10;---&gt; Slate/Gray Line: Cloud Management &amp; Monitoring (Route 53 Resolver, CloudWatch logs/metrics, session administration)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f1f5f9;strokeColor=#475569;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#1e293b;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
